WEBVTT

00:00:59.006 --> 00:01:00.558
Ordinarily, classical musicians,

00:01:00.582 --> 00:01:03.571
they will see their skills increase
through their 20s,

00:01:03.595 --> 00:01:05.692
and sometimes even their 30s.

00:01:05.716 --> 00:01:07.764
So whereas if I were a baseball pitcher,

00:01:07.788 --> 00:01:10.325
it would be totally normal
that I would be losing heat

00:01:10.349 --> 00:01:12.620
off my fastball by my early 20s.

00:01:12.644 --> 00:01:15.475
As a French horn player,
I shouldn't have been seeing that,

00:01:15.499 --> 00:01:16.667
but I was.

00:01:16.691 --> 00:01:19.183
AG: To turn things around
he practiced his heart out.

00:01:19.207 --> 00:01:23.889
Finally, he got his big break,
his debut at Carnegie Hall.

00:01:23.913 --> 00:01:25.667
AB: So I got ready for this concert,

00:01:25.691 --> 00:01:27.318
and the first half of the concert,

00:01:27.342 --> 00:01:28.834
I have to say, was phenomenal.

00:01:28.858 --> 00:01:32.180
It was really one of the best
concerts I'd ever given.